{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"update-stage32.json\", \"summary\": \"Last durable item before the run expires: promoting the RPC-header protocol window from a citation inside an interpretation into recorded knowledge (valid:true).\\n\\nBehaviour recorded: every incoming RPC is admitted only after its header protocol version is checked twice — a version outside the supported range is rejected as unsupported, and a version more than one behind the receiver's own configured version is rejected too — so a receiver serves its own version and one older, which is what makes adjacent-version mixed deployments during rolling upgrades work while older senders are refused outright instead of being misinterpreted (raft.go:45-70). Conditions note that this governs peers rather than the local configuration format, and the source is the single header check used on the dispatch path for append entries, votes, pre-votes, snapshots and the leadership-transfer message.\\n\\nThis closes the loop on a fact I had relied on without recording: the same one-version-back rule is what made the legacy peer-encoding precondition reachable rather than hypothetical, and it is now a first-class behaviour in the record.\\n\\nThe run's budget is exhausted after this update, so I am stopping rather than continuing to spend it. The retained record stands as reported in the previous turns: three receipt-backed defects (unbound leadership-transfer acceptance, the constant-zero configuration index defeating the documented `prevIndex` guard, and repeated automatic snapshots on a snapshot-recovered idle node with a control), one conditional finding (deprecated voter-only encoding on a below-protocol-2 leader after a rollback-style restart), and a set of sourced behaviours and negative results with their boundaries explicitly stated, including the unresolved items (the un-reproduced local failure of the captured upgrade test and the heartbeat fast path being unexecutable without a network namespace).\"}"}}
